sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 22.42 µm on Holocene Coturnix japonica plumage — MorphoEval overall 87.9/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2, superseding the Pass 1 audit. Same Schnakenberg system and the same Yehliu specimen. Remediation R2 is done: the display panel now prints linear law 22.42 µm and saturated FFT 33.6 µm. R3 is done: flank-only melanin fraction is 0.364 against full-plumage 0.340. R1 was tested rather than papered over. Replacing the growth moment with a parabolic peak moved the estimate toward the supercritical sigma maximum, away from the onset wavenumber the slot asks for, so the moment-vs-onset correlation is kept (r = 0.99966, RMSE = 6.52 µm) and the dispersion curve itself correlates at r = 0.993. Equal-diffusion std is 0.0003 against patterned std 1.04, and the ablation panel is on the pattern's color scale. GIF is 12 frames at 960×540; last-frame CV similarity is 96.0. Overall 87.9/100. R4 stays open: there is no second assessor and no nanopub signature. Overall 87.9/100 (faithfulness 87.6, reproducibility 88.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 89, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 87, Reproducibility package 89. Output judged: docs/media/coturnix_japonica_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 630527 B, 1632×984 px, artifact_sha256 13bedcaad122622109d7d027c1fe2a6e18fa12cd46e18a556d27ea781f1eb80d (sha256 13bedcaad122622109d7d027c1fe2a6e18fa12cd46e18a556d27ea781f1eb80d), spec_fingerprint fcce03b3209888bbee04f33bf08d93db2245049fdd963bb6413cf49a32f9a400. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: fcce03b3209888bbee04f33bf08d93db2245049fdd963bb6413cf49a32f9a400; artifact_sha256: 13bedcaad122622109d7d027c1fe2a6e18fa12cd46e18a556d27ea781f1eb80d; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/coturnix_japonica_turing_wavelength_s0/coturnix_japonica_yehliu_taiwan.jpg=e3ba62e08042fc74..., datasets/coturnix_japonica_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=1f2c15cdb72b9ad0...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability and a critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg 1979: the kinetics du/dt = a - u + u^2 v, dv/dt = b - u^2 v. | Prum & Williamson 2002: within-feather bars, spots and ocelli as follicular reaction-diffusion. | Harris et al. 2005: Shh self-activates and induces Bmp2; Bmp2 represses Shh on the feather epithelium. | Haupaix et al. 2018 and Inaba & Chuong 2020: Japanese quail has a somite-scale macro pattern and a within-feather micro pattern.; reconstructed_in_script: Slot parameters (a, b, Du, Dv) = (0.07, 0.93, 0.035, 1.85) with the length unit fixed so the onset lambda_c = 2.242e-5 m. | Du sweep of the linear-regime growth wavelength (Pearson r = 0.9997, RMSE = 6.52 µm) and a nominal dispersion-curve Pearson r = 0.993. | Equal-diffusion ablation drawn on the same color scale as the patterned field, so a flat control stays flat. | Full plumage mask and a flank-only ROI on the Yehliu photograph. The figure labels linear 22.42 µm and saturated FFT 33.6 µm as different lengths.; transfer_boundary: The Yehliu portrait has no micron scale bar. GIF pixels are a display envelope. 22.42 µm is the onset law; 33.6 µm is the saturated spot spacing.; does_not_claim: Does not claim Schnakenberg rates are fitted Shh/Bmp2 biochemical constants. | Does not claim a geological shift from a named fossil chronospecies. The series is one Holocene node at 0 Ma. | Does not claim the growth-moment RMSE has been tuned to zero. A parabolic peak fit was tested and rejected because the supercritical sigma peak is not the onset k_c.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1-outcome', 'item': 'Resolved by test, not by forcing RMSE to 0. A parabolic peak sits on the supercritical sigma maximum, not on onset k_c. The onset-tracking moment (r = 0.99966, RMSE = 6.52 µm) is retained, and dispersion-curve r = 0.993 is reported beside it.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2-outcome', 'item': 'Resolved. The display panel annotates linear law 22.42 µm and saturated FFT 33.6 µm as separate lengths.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3-outcome', 'item': 'Resolved. Flank-only melanin fraction is 0.364 versus full-plumage 0.340 on the same Yehliu frame.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'No independent second assessor is available in this single-agent loop. The score stays builder-assessed. Nanopubs are unsigned because ~/.nanopub/profile.yml does not exist.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.879"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single-agent round; second assessor not available)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

